  "text": {
    "card": "Seven-counter track: two sides take one or two in turn; the last counter wins.",
    "rules": "The gold meter shows counters remaining; red means first side and blue means second side. First side: one player. Second side: one to three players sharing its turn. First begins. Take one or two; taking the last counter wins. At zero counters the side opposite turn won. An empty pile ends the round; first may restart with seven. Each second-side player chooses a separate free stand: second_stand, second_back or second_far. Keep that stand for each turn.",
    "first_to_play": "First side\u2019s turn; wait for them to take counters.",
    "second_to_play": "Second side\u2019s turn; wait for them to take counters.",
    "join_first": "Join or accept the activity as the first side before taking counters.",
    "join_second": "Join or accept the activity as the second side before taking counters.",
    "other_side_missing": "Both sides must have a member before taking counters.",
    "not_enough": "There are not enough counters for that take. An empty pile ends the round.",
    "round_not_over": "Finish the current pile before restarting.",
